# Memory (global)

Durable findings from investigations — reference when the topic comes up.
Preferences live in AGENTS.md; this file is facts and proven techniques.

## This machine (Ubuntu 22.04, kernel 6.8.0-87-generic, 125 GiB RAM, RTX 3090)

### zswap — enabled, persisted, proven (2026-11-08)
- State: on, lzo/zbud, accept_compressed_ratio 90, max_pool_percent 20
- Params live ONLY in `/sys/module/zswap/parameters/` on this kernel — not
  under `/proc/sys`, so `sysctl.d` is a dead end here
- Persistence: `/usr/local/sbin/zswap-enable.sh` +
  `/etc/systemd/system/zswap-enable.service` (oneshot, enabled)
- Proof (root, via `/sys/kernel/debug/zswap` — mode 700): 512 MiB pageout →
  `stored_pages` 192 → 131264 (Δ exactly 131072 pages), readback → 192, data intact
- Counters that WORK on this kernel: `stored_pages` (sudo), per-VMA smaps
  `Swap:`, `swapon --show` USED (includes zswap-resident pages)
- Counters that LIE/absent here: `pswpin`/`pswpout` stay 0 for zswap pages;
  no `zswap*` in /proc/vmstat (no ZSWAP_STATS); `pool_*`/`entries` are n/a
  (ZSMALLOC_STAT off)
- `MADV_PAGEOUT=21` is correct on x86_64; an earlier `EINVAL` was a ctypes
  artifact — use raw C (mmap + madvise)
- Hold-mode test recipe: `sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK, SIGTERM)` BEFORE `sigwait`,
  else the default action kills the process (rc=143)
- Helpers (ephemeral, /tmp/opencode/): `zswap-roundtrip.c` (hold mode),
  `zswap-hold-proof.sh` (sudo driver), `zswap-setup.sh`

### OpenCode (V2)
- Repo layout: `opencode.json` is a symlinked user file (keep uncommitted);
  `cli.json` is a plain file in `~/.config/opencode` (not in the repo)
- Keybinds have NO double-tap/repeat mechanism (only key, press/release,
  `preventDefault`, `fallthrough`). `app.exit` override in cli.json =
  `["ctrl+d", "<leader>q"]` on purpose — Ctrl-C must not kill a session
- MCP V2 schema: `mcp.servers.<name>` with `type:"local"` + `command`;
  top-level `mcp.<name>` is deprecated
- npm `mcp-server-git` is dead (npm security-holder since 2026-08) → use
  `mcp-git@0.0.4` (bin `mcp-git`)
- MCP runtime: pin Node v26.13.0 bin dir in the config PATH — inherited PATH
  resolves node v18 first
- Config changes hot-reload (TUI included) — never tell the user to restart

### Powerline
- Canonical install = pipx venv; daemon liveness probe
  `pgrep -f 'bin/powerline-daemon'`; stale-kill needs argv0=python +
  `bin/powerline-daemon` + non-pipx path. Script: `script/install-powerline.sh`

## Tooling gotchas (this box)
- zsh shell wrapper mangles `[[ ]]` in one-liners → write multi-line scripts
  (see AGENTS.md)
- `swapon --show=NAME,USED` unsupported — use bare `swapon --show`
- `... | head` masks the real exit code — capture to a file, check rc
- `dmesg` denied as non-root (Operation not permitted)
- pgrep/pkill self-match: bracket trick `powerline[-]daemon` in manual commands
